# Auth Rules

Reference: `Documents/decisions/mobile-session-strategy.md`, `Documents/MOBILE_WEB_SESSION_IMPLEMENTATION.md`

## Stack

- Custom JWT (`ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET` / `REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET`) — not Firebase for login.
- Firebase is push-only (FCM) on mobile.

## Web

- httpOnly cookies: `AccessToken`, `RefreshToken`.
- `axios.defaults.withCredentials = true` via `setupAxios(axios)` in `main.jsx`.
- User object in localStorage: `{VITE_APP_NAME}-auth-v{version}` — never store refresh tokens there.
- Route guard: `RequireAuth` → `/auth/login`.
- Bootstrap: `GET /users/tenant-bootstrap` (non-blocking).

## Mobile

- Bearer token in memory + Expo SecureStore (`augmentik.mobile.*` keys).
- Refresh via `/users/refresh-access-token`; clear session on 401 after failed refresh.
- Device headers on every request: `x-device-id`, `x-app-platform`, `x-app-version`.
- Portal handoff: `/users/mobile-web-session/create|verify` + WebView `/mobile-entry?token=&tenant=&handoff=`.

## Backend

- `VerifyJwt` middleware accepts cookie or Bearer token.
- Production cookies: `secure` + `sameSite: 'none'` for cross-subdomain auth.

## Do's

- Extend `JWTProvider` / `AuthContext` — don't add parallel auth stacks.
- Normalize API base URL to avoid `/api/api/` duplication.
- Use `removeAuth` / `clearAllLocalAuth` on logout.

## Don'ts

- Don't skip `withCredentials` on auth or handoff calls.
- Don't put JWT secrets in frontend or mobile env.
- Don't store refresh tokens in localStorage on web.
